From 3b15351cf7545fe03251b8ef2a8437d10190923b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Hughes <ryan@heyoodle.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:43:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: quirks: disable CL states on the NVIDIA N1x host
 router

With CL states enabled on its links, the N1x host router runs the TMU
in uni-directional LowRes mode and only raises it to HiFi once a
DisplayPort tunnel has been activated, while the GPU is doing its first
link training. A monitor behind the tunnel (an LG 4K/240 Hz panel
behind a CalDigit TS4 here) then never syncs, drops HPD about 15 s
later, and the tunnel is torn down and set up again in a loop. On boot
this usually ends with the display left dark.

With CL states off the TMU stays in bi-directional HiFi mode from the
start, and the tunnel comes up at the first attempt, both with the dock
attached at boot and on hotplug.
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/quirks.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/quirks.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/quirks.c
index 9f7914ac2f..cc6938a789 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/quirks.c
@@ -114,6 +114,12 @@ static const struct tb_quirk tb_quirks[] = {
 	{ 0x0438, 0x0209, 0x0000, 0x0000, quirk_clx_disable },
 	{ 0x0438, 0x020a, 0x0000, 0x0000, quirk_clx_disable },
 	{ 0x0438, 0x020b, 0x0000, 0x0000, quirk_clx_disable },
+	/*
+	 * With CL states on the links of the NVIDIA N1x host router, a
+	 * monitor behind a DisplayPort tunnel never syncs to the first link
+	 * training and keeps dropping HPD.
+	 */
+	{ 0x0955, 0x1372, 0x0000, 0x0000, quirk_clx_disable },
 };
 
